// Data model of the theorem graph (theorems.html): theorems and conjectures of algebraic geometry (MSC 2020 14) and the
// premises of one chosen proof each, in English. Built on 3 November 2026 from the German files theorems.js and
// theorems-large.js of this folder, which stay unchanged for the older pages index.html and gross.html. The mapping of
// the old ids to the new ones is in reports/2026-11-03 Satzgraphen aller Gebiete/algebraic-geometry.md.
//
// Model (same as in all folders of graphs/, see the assignment in reports/2026-11-03 Satzgraphen aller Gebiete/):
//   theorems id, name, kind (axiom, theorem, lemma, corollary, conjecture), area, field, msc, msc5, premises, formula,
//            text, proof, concepts, year, who.
//            `area`: the three-character MSC class, as in the concept graph data/concept-graph.js; `msc5` the
//                    five-character class. "basic" for results from fields without a home folder (Hodge theory).
//            `premises`: the theorems that one usual textbook proof uses directly (named in `proof`); references to
//                    other folders carry a prefix ("ca:", "ct:", "st:") and point only to their anchor theorems.
//                    Conjectures have no premises and are never premises.
//            `concepts`: concepts of data/concept-graph.js that occur in the statement.
//            `proofName` (with optional `proofYear`, `proofWho`): name of the standard proof given by `premises` and
//                    `proof`; `alternativeProofs`: further proofs { name, premises, idea, year, who }, most important
//                    first, never circular; `foundation: true`: general tool of the area (3 November 2026).
// Theorems of commutative algebra (Nullstellensatz, Noether normalization, Krull, Artin–Rees, …) live in
// ../../commutative-algebra/ ("ca:"), those with first class 11 (Mordell–Weil, Hasse, Faltings) in
// ../../arithmetic-geometry/ ("ar:"); they are not repeated here.
//
// Prefix for references from other folders: "ag:<id>". Anchors: serre-vanishing, serre-duality, riemann-roch-curves,
// hurwitz-formula, bezout-theorem, weil-conjectures, zariski-main-theorem, grothendieck-vanishing.
// Sources for the proof paths: Hartshorne, Algebraic Geometry (1977); Mumford, Abelian Varieties (1970); Fulton,
// Intersection Theory (1984); Beauville, Complex Algebraic Surfaces (1983); Kollár and Mori, Birational Geometry of
// Algebraic Varieties (1998); Griffiths and Harris, Principles of Algebraic Geometry (1978); Milne, Lectures on Étale
// Cohomology (2013); Fantechi et al., FGA Explained (2005); Stacks Project. Years not checked.
// Not checked by a specialist.
// Checked by ../../tests/check-theorems.js.

