      proofName: "Dominating valuation rings (EGA II 7)", proofWho: "Grothendieck",
      formula: String.raw`\operatorname{Spec} K \to X,\ \operatorname{Spec} R \to Y \;\leadsto\; \operatorname{Spec} R \to X`,
      text: "Let f: X → Y be a morphism of finite type of Noetherian schemes. f is separated if and only if for every valuation ring R with fraction field K a morphism Spec R → Y has at most one lift Spec R → X extending a given Spec K → X; f is proper if and only if it has exactly one.",
